  "howItWorks": "How it works",
  "@howItWorks": {
    "description": "Раздел"
  },
  "howItWorksBody": "There are no accounts. Every device has its own key created on the device itself; devices recognize each other by these keys.\n\nDevices can only be linked with a QR code shown on screen: a stranger can neither connect nor send a file — such connections are rejected right away.\n\nFiles go directly between devices, encrypted (QUIC, TLS 1.3). If a direct path is impossible, data goes through a relay, which only sees the encrypted stream.\n\nAfter a connection drop the transfer resumes where it stopped, and every file is verified with a BLAKE3 hash.",
  "@howItWorksBody": {
    "description": "Пояснение"
  },
